@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "liferay.university.passport.access"

Feature: Liferay University Passport Access
	Testing the Liferay University Passport Access portlet.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                               |
	* I create a support user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                             |
	* I create a support user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.user1                       |
	| Email Address | passport.user1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                             |
	| Last Name     | User1                                |
	* I create a support user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.user2                      |
	| Email Address | passport.user2@pspartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                            |
	| Last Name     | User2                               |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I assign a user the email address "passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Passport Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| passport.user1@pscustomer.com.broken     |
	| passport.user2@pspartner.com.broken      |
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PASSAUTO |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Passport Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Request passport access as dxp customers
	New passports should be able to be requested by dxp customers.

	Given I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Passport Automotive |
	| Code                       | PASSAUTO            |
	| Type                       | Group               |
	| Industry                   | Automotive          |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner     |
	| Partner First Line Support | true                |
	| Tier                       | Premier             |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                  |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street     |
	| Country                    | United States       |
	| State                      | California          |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar         |
	| Zip                        | 91765               |
	| Region                     | US                  |
	| Language                   | English             |
	And I assign a user the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "PASSAUTO"
	And I assign a user the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "PASSAUTO"
	And I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "PASSAUTO"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the web organization "Customer"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the web organization "Customer"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the web organization "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the web organization "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	| Company Name           | Passport Automotive                      |
	| End User Email Address | passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	| Company Name           | Passport Automotive                      |
	| End User Email Address | passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |

